5. What is the output? Explain the exception chaining.
public class Q5 {
    public static void method3() throws Exception {
        throw new RuntimeException("Root cause");
    }
    public static void method2() {
        try { method3(); }
        catch (Exception e) {
            throw new IllegalStateException("Method2 failed", e);
        }
    }
    public static void main(String[] args) {
        try { method2(); }
        catch (IllegalStateException e) {
            System.out.println(e.getMessage());
            System.out.println(e.getCause().getMessage());
        }
    }
}

6. Rewrite this code using try-with-resources and fix the resource leak:
public String readAndProcess(String path) {
    FileInputStream fis = null;
    BufferedReader br = null;
    try {
        fis = new FileInputStream(path);
        br = new BufferedReader(new InputStreamReader(fis));
        return br.readLine();
    } catch (IOException e) {
        return null;
    } finally {
        try { if (br != null) br.close(); }
        catch (IOException ignore) {}
    }
    // BUG: fis is never closed if br creation fails!
}
